  "gotchas": [
    "Only deliver the product or grant access once this returns SUCCESS.",
    "A PENDING payment is re-checked against the gateway on each call, so the status can change between two calls.",
    "Every response is wrapped in the same envelope: read the payload from data, and on failure read error.message and error.code.",
    "Only PENDING, SUCCESS and FAILED occur in practice: CANCELLED exists in the data model but no flow reaches it today, so treat it as a non-successful terminal state without expecting it.",
    "For accounting, never use the requested amount alone: what left the payer and what you receive depend on fee_charge_mode. Read debited_amount and net_amount, or the amounts object (requested, fee, charged, net)."
  ],
  "evidence": {
    "spans": [
      "https://api.saspay.me/api/v1/payments/{payment_id}/verify/",
      "Ne livrez un produit ou n'activez un accès que lorsque `GET /payments/{payment_id}/verify/` renvoie `SUCCESS`.",
      "Si le statut connu est `PENDING`, revérifie toujours l'état réel côté gateway avant de répondre",
      "Toutes les réponses de l'API partagent la même enveloppe, qu'il s'agisse d'un succès ou d'une erreur.",
      "en pratique, seuls `PENDING`, `SUCCESS` et `FAILED` apparaissent.",
      "Pour rapprocher votre comptabilité, utilisez `charged` (ce qui a quitté le compte du client) et `net_amount` (ce qui vous revient) — jamais `amount` seul."
